===Etymology 1===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro|ine-pro}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|schicken|t=to outfit oneself, fit in, arrange appropriately}}, from {{der|de|goh|*skihhen}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*skikkijan}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*skikkijaną|t=to order, send}}. This represents the causative of {{cog|gmh|geschehen}}, {{m|gmh|geschehen|geschēn|t=to happen, rush}}.

Akin to {{cog|enm|skekken|t=to send forth}}, {{cog|ang|sċēon|t=to happen}}, {{cog|nl|schielijk|schie-}} in {{m|nl|schielijk|t=hasty}}. Related to {{m+|en|chic}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|ditransitive}} to [[send]], to [[dispatch]] (a person, letter, money etc. to a destination or a person)
#: {{syn|de|senden|versenden|verschicken}}
#: {{ant|de|empfangen|erhalten|bekommen}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie hat mir einen Liebesbrief '''geschickt'''.|She '''sent''' me a love letter.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[hurry]] (rare)
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to be decent, to be appropriate
#: {{syn|de|[[benehmen|sich benehmen]]}}

